            <ArticleTitle>[An 82 year old patient with severe abdominal pain and air in the portal vein].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>368-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00108-008-2258-x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 82 year old male patient presented with acute abdominal pain. Computer tomography revealed portomesenteric vein gas and a paralytic ileus due to an acute mesenteric ischemia. Because of the presence of peritoneal signs immediate surgical exploration was performed. The diagnosis of a non-occlusive mesenteric ischemia with bowel infarction was confirmed during surgery and pathologically. The patient survived without any severe consequences.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
